# How the board draws, and how you move
// The board is a grid of its squares, each square shows its piece:  styles.css colors them.
// Drag a piece onto a square the rules allow:  the square lights up as you hold it there.
// Or click a piece, then click where it should go:  every square it can go to lights up.

a piece
	to draw it
		-- a king wears a crown
		if it is a king
			<icon name="crown" />

	on click
		-- picked, to move with the next click;  a second click puts it down
		set board to the board of its square
		if the picked piece of board is it
			set the picked piece of board to nothing
		otherwise if it can move and it is yours
			set the picked piece of board to it

a square
	its "lit" is
		-- Whether the picked piece can go there:  it lights up (styles.css)
		yes if the picked piece of its board exists and the picked piece of its board can go to it
		no otherwise

	to draw it
		-- its piece, and a dot where the picked piece can go
		<children />
		if its lit is yes
			<icon name="circle" class="Target" color="yellow" />

	its pieces are draggable when the piece can move and the piece is yours
	it is droppable when the piece can go to it

	when a piece is dropped
		move the piece to the square

	on click
		-- a click where the picked piece can go moves it there
		if its lit is yes
			move the picked piece of its board to it
